# BYD Seal four-door electric saloon, 2023 onwards.
#
# The Seal: the low four-door saloon on the e-Platform 3.0 with the 82.5 kWh
# Blade battery, the sloping fastback roof and the full-width tail lamp bar.
# UK prices were confirmed on 1 September 2023.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BYD_Seal
#
# Dimensions 4.800 x 1.875 x 1.460 m, wheelbase 2.920 m (BYD UK media
# specification table, 1 September 2023). The width over mirrors is 2.150 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side elevation was obtainable. Image 1 is
# about 20 degrees off the side axis at about 1.3 m, so the flank is estimated
# within the published dimensions and the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (b) for two names only. Shadow Green and Indigo Grey are
# named by Autocar on 26 January 2024 as premium paints; White and Black are
# plain names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
#
# Speed 180 km/h. Comfort 90/315, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 90. Classes 2,3.
# Dates: intro September 2023, when UK prices were confirmed; retires
# staggered 2046-2049.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/byd-seal.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/byd-seal.dae. References:
# citycars/references/byd-seal/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the flank is estimated from an oblique photograph. The
# flush handles, running-light internals and diffuser vanes are simplified.
# The proud panoramic glazing adds about 14 mm above the nominal painted roof
# height.


obj=citycar
name=BYDSeal(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2023
intro_month=11
retire_year=2049
retire_month=6
speed=180
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=90
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=315

